From f0d5c11523424144edea79240064f15d079fd5ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:00:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: Add system sleep PM ops

pvr_pm_ops only has runtime PM callbacks. On system suspend the GPU stays
runtime-active with its firmware running while the power domain goes down,
and the first runtime PM get after resume fails with -EINVAL
("pvr_power_get returned error -22, attempting recovery"). The recovery
can end in "GPU device lost" with the client stuck.

Route system sleep through the runtime PM callbacks with
pm_runtime_force_suspend()/pm_runtime_force_resume(), so the firmware is
stopped and the GPU powered down before sleep and brought back after.

Tested on the TrimUI Smart Pro (A133, GE8300): vkcube (60 frames) works
before suspend and after each of three s2idle cycles, with no pvr errors.
Before, the first render after one suspend cycle lost the device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: leow149 <leow149@lucidmail.xyz>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
index 5c965ef02..12978f70d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_drv.c
@@ -1516,6 +1516,12 @@ static const struct of_device_id dt_match[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, dt_match);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops pvr_pm_ops = {
+	/*
+	 * System sleep goes through the runtime PM callbacks, so that the
+	 * firmware is stopped and the GPU powered down properly before the
+	 * power domain goes off, and brought back up on resume.
+	 */
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(pvr_power_device_suspend, pvr_power_device_resume, pvr_power_device_idle)
 };
 
